% `write_term_to_string/1` from `library(meta)`: the inverse of the
% reader pinned by `read_term_test`. The result is a string, so the
% cases pin the *surface spelling* the printer produces — compound
% syntax, string quoting, and `_` for an unbound variable — rather than
% a term structure. The compiler's own printer is already covered by
% `atom_quoting`; what this directory adds is the host-call path itself.
%
% The data the goals hand over (`f`, `hello`) is deliberately left
% undeclared: the renamer would qualify a declared constructor to
% `write_term_test:f`, and the cases pin the unqualified surface
% spelling. The `compound` goal therefore emits YCHR-20101, so the
% directory is in `expectsWarnings` (test/YCHR/GoldenTest.hs) and
% `WERROR_EXEMPT` (test/scheme/test_golden.py).
:- module(write_term_test, [go/2]).

:- use_module(library(meta)).

:- chr_constraint go/2.

go(T, R) <=> R is write_term_to_string(T).
